{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "FULL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.5,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 2.25,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver — this provisional ruling was made without human review and either party may appeal it once under POL-GEN-04. The SGD 4.50 no-show fee charged on trip TRP-02714 is refunded in full to the rider, and the driver is paid a platform-funded goodwill sum of SGD 2.25. The two are independent: the goodwill is charged to the platform and is never recovered from the rider, and it does not reduce the rider's refund.\n\nWhy the fee is refunded. A no-show fee stands only if the driver actually reached the pickup point (POL-NS-01). On EV-GPS-02714 — 97 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps — the driver's closest approach to the pickup pin was 272.98 m, and the derived count of fixes inside the 150 m arrival radius for this TRANSPORT_HUB pickup is 0. The trace shows no qualifying in-radius fix in the 15 minutes before the cancellation, so POL-NS-02 puts the driver outside the geofence, POL-NS-01 limb (b) fails, and the fee is not chargeable. The 'I'm Here' tap recorded at 09:19:17 on EV-TRIP-02714 is a status the driver set and cannot supply the in-geofence arrival that limb (b) requires; POL-NS-01 limb (c) measures the dwell from the first qualifying in-geofence fix (0 s here, a 180 s shortfall), not from the tap. EV-FARE-02714 shows the SGD 4.50 line charged with nothing returned (cancellation_fee 4.50, total_charged 4.50, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00), and it reconciles with platform_policy.cancellation_fee_sgd of SGD 4.50, so the whole SGD 4.50 goes back to the rider.\n\nWhy the driver still receives SGD 2.25. His closest point, 272.98 m, lies outside the arrival radius but inside the 400 m ceiling POL-NS-03 draws, and POL-NS-05's own closing sentence sends a driver stationary within 300 m of the pin but outside the arrival radius to POL-NS-03. Neither party named an entrance, block, tower or bay in EV-CHAT-02714 ('im here' / 'cant see you' / 'im here already, where are you'), and trip_record.registered_pickup_points is 2, so POL-NS-03(ii) attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity rather than to either party and fixes a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee — SGD 2.25, the goodwill figure carried on EV-FARE-02714. POL-NS-03(i) does not apply because the rider stated no sub-location.\n\nWhat is not payable. POL-NS-07's full driver compensation of SGD 3.60 (80 percent of SGD 4.50) is not payable: POL-NS-07 requires POL-NS-01 to be satisfied in full, and limb (b) fails. The anti-farming check would not withhold it in any event — EV-DPROF-02714 shows 1 no-show termination against 137 completed trips in 30 days (0.007), below both limbs.\n\nClaims addressed. The Driver Advocate's claim that POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full is rejected: it rests on the driver's own arrival tap and the platform wait timer, and limb (b) fails on the GPS trace, which the tap cannot replace. The Driver Advocate's alternative claim for human review under POL-NS-09(b) is rejected: the policy resolves the arrival question for precisely this situation — POL-NS-02 and POL-NS-01(c) define arrival and dwell by the GPS trace — so there is no direct contradiction the policy leaves open, and no POL-NS-09 trigger fires. POL-NS-05 does not fire (no fix is matched to the 09:19:17 marker and 272.98 m is short of its 300 m line), so the arrival marker is not recorded as a false arrival and no POL-NS-05(ii) referral is made. Both advocates agree POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider — the driver replied 50 seconds after the rider's message (09:20:57 to 09:21:47), inside the 120-second limit — and the residual mislocation is decided under POL-NS-03 as above. The Driver Advocate is right that POL-GEN-01 bars the lifetime counter prior_no_show_flags from carrying any finding; it has not been used.\n\nWeight, confidence and discarded evidence. Every artifact that carries a deciding fact is COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0 (EV-GPS-02714, EV-TRIP-02714, EV-CHAT-02714, EV-FARE-02714), so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and confidence is set at 0.85, above the 0.70 floor. There is no clock skew, trace gap, chat gap or fare mismatch under POL-NS-08. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02714-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0; it carries no fact and is cited only for its absence, so it does not cap confidence, and POL-NS-06(i) accumulation is unavailable. A rider claim that the 180 s shortfall refunds the fee under POL-NS-06 was discarded before the hearing for not disclosing the advisory's MISSING_ARTIFACT issue code; the same refund follows independently from POL-NS-02, so nothing turns on it. The monetary effect is SGD 4.50 + SGD 2.25 = SGD 6.75, below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so the ruling executes automatically."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Independently of arrival, POL-NS-01 limb (c) requires a continuous in-geofence dwell of at least the free waiting period in force - 180 seconds on this trip, read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec (no_show_threshold_sec is null) - and POL-NS-06 refunds the fee in full where the effective in-geofence dwell falls short. The measured dwell is 0.0 seconds (derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec), a shortfall of 180.0 seconds (derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.shortfall_sec). Limb (i) of POL-NS-06 cannot help the driver: there were no in-geofence intervals to accumulate (derived.arrival.accumulated_dwell.run_count = 0), and the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02714-01 is MISSING with admissibility status MISSING and weight_multiplier 0.0 - I rely on that artifact only for its absence, and no advisory covering this pickup road exists, so limb (i) is simply unavailable and the shortfall stands.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason_code": "IMPAIRMENT_UNDISCLOSED",
      "detail": "the claim cites impaired artifact EV-ADVIS-02714-01 at weight_multiplier 0.0 but does not name its issue code(s): MISSING_ARTIFACT"
    }
  ]
}
